it is  january 3rd 2022  and it's time for another monthly update  video in which i'm going to talk about  what we've got coming up in january and  what you might have missed in december  just in case you want to put that on  your radar or go back to it i also did a  end of the year recap video so i'm not  going to talk about the whole year of  2021 you can go to that video which is  linked to below  if you would like to learn more about  that  so with no further ado three big things  coming up this month  my academic classes begin at least at  one of the places that i'm teaching  milwaukee institute of art and design  and so i'm gearing up for that and  shooting some new video content and  doing a lot of behind the scenes kind of  things  big thing number two those of you who  have been  patiently waiting for  new self-directed study videos to come  out i'm going to start doing those again  this month with one on augustine  and big thing number three if you don't  already know about stoicism today  selected writings volume three you  notice this is a proof copy that's why  it says not for resale  that came out in december and it's got a  lot of really great essays it's uh  co-edited by me and leah goldrick so you  might want to check that out if you have  any interest in stoicism you're going to  find a lot of really great  discussions of it how-to's even some  controversies  in there so let's talk now about  december and then we will jump into  january  so what did december hold well my  academic classes predictably enough all  came to a close there was a bit of drama  at the milwaukee institute of art and  design because the course management  system closed completely for not  technical college but available did  teach a class for carthage college and  that one came out okay as well grades  all got in  the students who are  taking incompletes are finishing them up  as we speak in december  we also for christmas did something  completely different and when i say we i  mean my wife andy and our cat sassy and  i we went up to green bay because at a  gala event we had bid on some packers  tickets for  christmas  and we actually won and so we drove up  to green bay on the 24th stayed in a  hotel got sassy situated  took her a little while to settle in the  first night she actually was up and down  and i had to attend her about every two  hours but uh all told it was pretty good  we went to the game packers won in a  very close game lots of fun drove down  the next day so that was our christmas  and we had a very low-key new year  as well  um i did you know my my usual events  my ask me anything session my public  hegel q a session  scott truly and i did a great session  for um  for classic metal class uh and i also  did the political theory and practice  discussion all of those are linked to  below if you want to see them  and we got two sessions of wisdom for  life in also two sessions of drive time  for river west in which i  um interviewed some some guests  including sam from southpaw podcast and  um  dan from the recombination area here in  milwaukee  as i mentioned you know i had classes  going on and and i also had a lot of  client work in december as well  including some new clients  um so i'm you know once again quite  blessed and that i do zero marketing or  uh promotion and clients find their way  to me for philosophical counseling  tutorials consulting  and various other things um video work  uh i got three half hour hegel videos  done not uh  not exactly what i wanted but at least i  got those done and  core concept videos i got to some  foucault videos that i'd been meaning to  do for a long time on the subject and  power  um finished out the  speculative fiction studies with uh  videos about leguins earthy books i i  know i had stuff on tahanu this last  month maybe also about the farthest  shore  there's also a video of an event that i  took part in with my friend and  collaborator harold covley  about pro races determining pro-racist  for the second brazilian epictetus  symposium hosted by aldo dinucci and  that was that was quite good  um  did some some interesting things using  the wombo ai art generator i did two  videos one using my full name gregory  bryant ignatius sadler and the other one  using the title of my  senior honors thesis isomorphic truth  self-referential statement groups and  you know they produced some interesting  art that i commented on  um we did worlds of speculative fiction  uh  but it wasn't a session instead it was  all about the voting for who's going to  be you know in the running this this  coming year  and then um  i did one sadler's honest reviews on  elliot rosenstocks the hyper state and  uh  it's uh  what is it the hyperstate and it's being  or something like that i don't have the  book right in front of me  podcast episodes i did a lot of podcast  episodes and these are for my my ethics  class on aristotle's nick mccann ethics  books eight and nine on friendship and  relationships in general and there's a  lot of cool stuff in there that i think  i'm going to go back to  then i did a sequence of three on peter  singer and his book the most good that  you can do and then finished it up with  some stuff from my existentialism class  on serving kierkegaard's the present age  so that was december and it kind of  limped to a halt  and i didn't get as much done as i would  have liked but you know i can say that  about just about every month  all right what do we have coming up in  january so the first thing i want to put  on your radar is two different dates  the 5th and the 19th those are  wednesdays from 4 to 6 pm central time  i will be on the air with drive time  from river west river west is our  community radio station here in  milwaukee but you can hear it anywhere  in the world by going to  riverwestradio.com link is below and you  can hear me and the co-host discussing  the news of the day and also  interviewing some very interesting  people  on the 8th at  noon i'll be hold holding my usual ama  that's ask me anything  session  also on the 8th at 2 pm for patreon  supporters i will be having my  philosophy  chat session  on the 12th at 5 p.m that's a wednesday  we'll have the public hegel q a  and discussion session  then on the 15th  at  noon classic metal class scott truly and  i have got a whole bunch of cool topics  lined up in advance that we're going to  be  talking about and uh delving into so  you're welcome to join us for that uh  people can ask questions make comments  and we respond to them  as we're going through it  on the 20th uh is uh  at noon is going to be the first live  reading of the month from my book this  is live reading number 18 from  reason fulfilled by revelation the 1930s  christian philosophy debates in france  we're still in the blondel section so  we'll be talking about that quite a bit  i'll read and then we discuss the  materials  on the 22nd at 12 p.m we have the first  worlds of speculative fiction  uh session of the  season of the year you could say and i  will be discussing  uh stevenson's anathem a book that i  have been plowing my way through it's  nearly a thousand pages for quite a  while and been putting off for a while  we're going to kick off  2022 with with that  and that takes place with a video  premiere at noon and then around 1 30  sometimes 1 40 depending how long the  video goes  i'll be having a live  session with people  do doing video conferencing talking  about it on the 23rd the next day at  noon we have our political theory and  practice discussion and you know given  all the um discussion that i've been  having in common some of it productive  some of it very unproductive about  foucault and power i think i'm going to  actually do something about  foucault and power relations  for that discussion  then on the 27th we've got two things  going on at noon we have our live  reading again from my book reason  fulfilled by revelation  and at 6 00 p.m milwaukee stoic  fellowship anybody's welcome because  it's a zoom session so if you've got an  interest in stoicism you can show up but  you do want to of course make sure you  do some of the cicero reading that we're  going to be discussing then finally on  the 29th at noon i will be  doing my self-directed study  in philosophy video on augustine we'll  do a video premiere which means that you  can watch it be one of the first people  to enjoy it and then  i'll be answering questions in live chat  about that  what else do we get going on that's a  busy month thank thank goodness we've  got like you know 31 days to it although  we've already burned through too  i got to get my classes up and running  because classes open up a day from to a  week from today  for my milwaukee institute of art and  design i've got a little bit more lead  time for the medieval philosophy class  that i'm teaching for carthage because  they have a j term which i'm not  teaching in so february i've got to be  ready for that medieval philosophy class  um i got a lot of client work to do you  know i've i'm a little bit behind on  correspondence there have been people  who have emailed me and i i have to get  back to them about you know  philosophical counseling or tutorials or  things like that  i'm also leading a reading group on  seneca that that meets four times  i think it may be past the deadline to  sign up for that it's been advertised on  my social media and in other places  um that's going to go on the the course  of this month not this monday but every  monday after this i'm hoping to do a lot  of writing this month as well  and of course i'm gonna be doing things  to promote stoicism today selected  writings volume  three uh we might have some interviews  with authors or some other cool stuff  going on maybe in the blog maybe in my  video channel maybe in other  venues  and then uh video work so  obviously half hour hegel we're now in  the revealed religion section i'd like  to keep making some headway there i'd  like to get my six videos for the month  done i'd like to get some sadler's  honest reviews done so far i've been  getting like one a month i'd like to  jack that up to about four a month so i  can start getting caught up on things  core concept videos i've got one more  foucault video to release and then i've  got to start shooting core concept  videos for my medieval philosophy class  so that means some cool new stuff on  augustine  and boethius i don't know if the  boethius will be released by the end of  the month  um but i'll certainly be shooting at  this this month i've also got to release  some of the le guin um  earth sea stuff that i i didn't get to  there's actually two whole books yet to  release so this month i will be  releasing videos on tales from earthsea  and then you know i'll do some more of  the wombo ai stuff there'll be videos  from the events and sessions that i'm  doing and i'll do some more sadler's  stories videos most likely i've got some  things to reminisce about that some of  you may be  interested in and we'll see what other  kinds of videos i want to shoot  podcast you know i'm still releasing  stuff on kierkegaard that i produced for  my existentialism class  i've got to do some stuff on nietzsche's  genealogy taking the videos that i  produced a while back and converting  them  to  podcast episodes taking out all the um  and things like that  and then you might see some augustine  podcast episodes come out as well  and that's pretty much taking us up to  the end so i hope that you're having a  good beginning of the new year i mean  nobody knows what's going to happen with  omicron and you know all the stuff that  you know  dislocations economically and things  like that that we're facing but  you know hopefully we can still have a  decent year  and learn a lot of stuff and engage in  some some good discussions and i hope to  see you at some of these online events  and you know maybe someday we'll be back  to  face-to-face events would be which would  be kind of nice and kind of cool  wouldn't it so  that's uh it from from me and uh  yeah happy new year to all of you  you

